  "generated_text": "First, we rewrite the given equation:\n\\[556 x22 + 77 = 89x - 8\\]\n\n\nNext, we rearrange the equation to bring all terms on one side:\n\\[56x^2 - 89xx 85 = 0\\]\n\n\nWe can factor out the common term $x$:\n\\[x(56x - 89) = 0\\]\n\n\n\n\n\nThis gives us two possible solutions:\n\\[x = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 56x - 89 = 0\\]\n\n\nSolving the second equation for $x$:\n\\[56x - 89 = 0\\]\n\\[56x = 89\\]\n\\[x = \\frac{89}{56}\\]\n\n\nTherefore, the other value of $x$ that solves the equation is:\n\\[\\boxed{\\frac{89}{56}}\\]",
  "grade": {
